{
  "schema": "prova.verification-case/1",
  "title": "EBIC graphical lasso network",
  "description": "The EBIC graphical lasso network of ten items of psych::bfi (A1-A5, C1-C5; 2,632 complete rows), from Pearson correlations. Both sides: gamma = 0.5, 100 penalties spaced on the log scale from max|r| down to 0.01 x max|r|, diagonal not penalized, no thresholding, the regularized network returned (no unregularized refit). psychnets uses its own solver (native = TRUE) and returns the optimum at the selected penalty; qgraph uses the glasso package, here with its convergence threshold tightened from the default 1e-4 to 1e-10 (thr, passed through EBICglasso's dots) so that the two solvers can be read against each other. All 45 node pairs are compared, the zeros included, and the selected penalty.",
  "covers": [
    "ebic_glasso()"
  ],
